From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 11:01:52 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] sidebar: a collapsed project counts a thread waiting for an
 answer

A collapsed project group's header shows how many of its threads wait for
the user. Upstream counts a pending question there since #66708, under the
same badge as a permission prompt, because both read WaitingForConfirmation.
0030 gave a pending question a status of its own, WaitingForAnswer -- and
0072 gave the same status to a thread whose subagent waits for the user --
but the header's two counting loops (one for an expanded group, one for a
collapsed one) still matched WaitingForConfirmation alone. So a collapsed
project hid exactly the threads that were waiting on the user, where stock
Zed shows them. Found by the upstream-native review of 2026-11-15
(docs/UPSTREAM-NATIVE-REVIEW.md in the hub, defect 2).

Both loops now count either status. The header's tooltip keeps upstream's
wording, "waiting for confirmation", which upstream itself uses for a
question.

Test: sidebar_child_background_tests'
test_child_background_collapsed_header_counts_a_thread_waiting_for_an_answer,
with two rig helpers, project_header and collapse_project (Red on the series
before this patch). A child waiting for the user reads the same status as
0030's question, so it stands in for one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---

diff --git a/crates/sidebar/src/sidebar.rs b/crates/sidebar/src/sidebar.rs
index ed604be..d7ab96c 100644
--- a/crates/sidebar/src/sidebar.rs
+++ b/crates/sidebar/src/sidebar.rs
@@ -2225,7 +2225,13 @@ impl Sidebar {
                     if info.status == AgentThreadStatus::Running {
                         has_running_threads = true;
                     }
-                    if info.status == AgentThreadStatus::WaitingForConfirmation {
+                    // A thread waiting for an answer (0030) is counted as a permission prompt is,
+                    // as upstream counts a pending question since #66708 (0129).
+                    if matches!(
+                        info.status,
+                        AgentThreadStatus::WaitingForConfirmation
+                            | AgentThreadStatus::WaitingForAnswer
+                    ) {
                         waiting_thread_count += 1;
                     }
                     live_info_by_session.insert(info.session_id.clone(), info);
@@ -2258,7 +2264,13 @@ impl Sidebar {
                     if info.status == AgentThreadStatus::Running {
                         has_running_threads = true;
                     }
-                    if info.status == AgentThreadStatus::WaitingForConfirmation {
+                    // A thread waiting for an answer (0030) is counted as a permission prompt is,
+                    // as upstream counts a pending question since #66708 (0129).
+                    if matches!(
+                        info.status,
+                        AgentThreadStatus::WaitingForConfirmation
+                            | AgentThreadStatus::WaitingForAnswer
+                    ) {
                         waiting_thread_count += 1;
                     }
                     // Resolve the thread_id for this session so we can
diff --git a/crates/sidebar/src/sidebar_child_background_tests.rs b/crates/sidebar/src/sidebar_child_background_tests.rs
index 48ae393..55c6ca0 100644
--- a/crates/sidebar/src/sidebar_child_background_tests.rs
+++ b/crates/sidebar/src/sidebar_child_background_tests.rs
@@ -210,6 +210,36 @@ impl Rig {
     }
 }
 
+impl Rig {
+    /// The project group's header row: its key and the count of threads it says are waiting.
+    fn project_header(&self, cx: &mut VisualTestContext) -> (ProjectGroupKey, usize) {
+        self.sidebar.read_with(cx, |sidebar, _cx| {
+            sidebar
+                .contents
+                .entries
+                .iter()
+                .find_map(|entry| match entry {
+                    ListEntry::ProjectHeader {
+                        key,
+                        waiting_thread_count,
+                        ..
+                    } => Some((key.clone(), *waiting_thread_count)),
+                    _ => None,
+                })
+                .expect("the project's header is listed")
+        })
+    }
+
+    /// Collapses the project group, as a click on its header does.
+    fn collapse_project(&self, cx: &mut VisualTestContext) {
+        let (key, _) = self.project_header(cx);
+        self.sidebar.update_in(cx, |sidebar, window, cx| {
+            sidebar.toggle_collapse(&key, window, cx);
+        });
+        cx.run_until_parked();
+    }
+}
+
 /// The child reports a state; no parent event follows.
 fn report(child: &Entity<AcpThread>, state: acp_v2::StateUpdate, cx: &mut VisualTestContext) {
     child
@@ -435,3 +465,30 @@ async fn test_child_background_waiting_child_reads_waiting_for_answer(cx: &mut T
     report(&first, running(), cx);
     assert_eq!(rig.status(cx), AgentThreadStatus::Background);
 }
+
+/// A collapsed project's header counts a thread that waits for an answer. Stock Zed counts a
+/// pending question there since #66708, under the same "waiting" badge as a permission prompt;
+/// 0030 gave the question a status of its own, and the header's two counting loops matched
+/// `WaitingForConfirmation` only, so a collapsed project hid a thread waiting on the user
+/// (upstream-native review, defect 2). A child waiting for the user reads the same status, so it
+/// stands in for the question here.
+#[gpui::test]
+async fn test_child_background_collapsed_header_counts_a_thread_waiting_for_an_answer(
+    cx: &mut TestAppContext,
+) {
+    let (rig, cx) = rig(true, cx).await;
+    let child = rig.spawn_child("child", cx);
+    report(&child, waiting(), cx);
+    assert_eq!(
+        rig.status(cx),
+        AgentThreadStatus::WaitingForAnswer,
+        "fixture"
+    );
+
+    rig.collapse_project(cx);
+    let (_, waiting_threads) = rig.project_header(cx);
+    assert_eq!(
+        waiting_threads, 1,
+        "the collapsed header counts the thread that waits for an answer"
+    );
+}
